moral_relevance_raw:
2

This scenario centers on a technical/administrative change—a shift in internal file-naming conventions for intake records—which is fundamentally a practical/operational matter, not a moral one.

The moral-adjacent element is thin: the director "did not care at all about the effect this would have on staff," which gestures toward indifference to employee impact. However, the actual effect described is limited to a file-naming format change in tracking software—an inconvenience or workflow adjustment, not a harm to wellbeing, rights, fairness, or dignity. There's no indication staff face job loss, unsafe conditions, discrimination, or exploitation;
